# Architecture brainstorm prompt maintenance

When you make **significant** player-facing or design-contract changes in this project, update [`docs/architecture_brainstorm_prompt.md`](docs/architecture_brainstorm_prompt.md) in the same change set so external-AI brainstorm context stays accurate.

## Update when you
- Add/change/remove an architecture, economy policy, special (Q), primitives, starting tags, or base resists
- Materially change combat loops (parry, shield, combos, dash economy, heat/vent, blood harvest, RAM/drones)
- Add/change statuses, synergies, craft recipes, loot parts, or tag gates that affect build identity
- Change campaign/tutorial/procedural route shape, acts, or biome set in a way that affects setting pitch
- Add a new faction/behavior pillar that changes how architectures should counter content
- Change design pillars or extensibility rules described in `docs/systems.md`

## How to update
- Keep the fenced copy-paste prompt block as the source of truth for external AIs
- Patch only the sections that drifted (architectures, synergies, routes, crafts, constraints)
- Preserve the response-format / brainstorm goals unless those instructions intentionally change
- Prefer factual current behavior over aspirational wishlist; mark open gaps as design tension if useful
- Do not invent lore or mechanics that are not in the game or design docs

## Skip when
- Pure refactors, renames, bugfixes, or UI polish with no design-facing change
- Tiny number tweaks that do not change the fantasy or identity of a system
- Changes already fully reflected in the prompt

## Do not skip
Shipping a significant architecture/economy/content identity change without refreshing this prompt is a miss — amend it before finishing (alongside the manual QA checklist when that also applies).
